                I'm an IT Engineering student who likes taking systems apart to understand how
                they actually work &mdash; whether that's a microcontroller circuit, a network
                packet, or a plant's SCADA setup. My curiosity started with hardware: building
                Arduino projects like ultrasonic sensors and motor controllers taught me how
                software meets the physical world. That same instinct now pulls me toward
                cyber security &mdash; I want to understand not just how systems are built,
                but how they can be broken, and how to defend them.
            </p>
            <p class="about-text reveal">
                Originally from Mustang, Nepal, I've since studied and lived across very
